  "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x=2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={50}^{\u2218}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2\\cdot {50}^{\u2218}) & =2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{50}^{\u2218}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{50}^{\u2218} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}\u2061({100}^{\u2218}) & =2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{50}^{\u2218}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{50}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{100}^{\u2218}\\operatorname{tan}\u2061{50}^{\u2218}}{2-2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{50}^{\u2218}} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{50}^{\u2218}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{50}^{\u2218}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061{50}^{\u2218}}{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{50}^{\u2218}}}{2-2\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{50}^{\u2218}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{sin}^{2}\u2061{50}^{\u2218}}{2(1-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{50}^{\u2218})} \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}\u2061{50}^{\u2218}}{1-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{50}^{\u2218}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing  the Pythagorean identity ${sin}^{2}\u2061{50}^{\u2218}=1-{cos}^{2}\u2061{50}^{\u2218},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sin}^{2}\u2061{50}^{\u2218}}{1-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{50}^{\u2218}} & =\\frac{1-{cos}^{2}\u2061{50}^{\u2218}}{1-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{50}^{\u2218}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(1-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{50}^{\u2218})(1+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{50}^{\u2218})}{1-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{50}^{\u2218}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(1-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{50}^{\u2218})}(1+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{50}^{\u2218})}{\\cancel{1-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{50}^{\u2218}}} \\\\  & =1+\\operatorname{cos}\u2061{50}^{\u2218}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
